   "title": "Typical termination for output driver and device evaluation",
   "page": 5,
   "description": "One differential output pair drives two 50 Ω transmission lines to a differential receiver. At the receiver end each line is terminated by a 50 Ω resistor to VTT, which sits 2.0 V below VCC. The same load, 50 Ω to VCC − 2.0 V, is the one the DC and AC output figures are measured with.",
