 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Function",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Two independent channels. Each takes a single-ended LVTTL/LVCMOS level on D and drives the matching Q and /Q pair at LVPECL levels referred to the 3.3 V supply. No supply other than +3.3 V and ground is needed; VCC may be 3.0 V to 3.6 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Open inputs",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "With its D input left unconnected a channel's Q output goes HIGH. The inputs have no internal pull-up or pull-down resistor; they are PNP stages, so they draw little current from the driving logic."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Output levels and loading",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "The LVPECL outputs are specified into 50 Ω returned to VCC − 2.0 V. VOH and VOL track VCC one for one; at VCC = 3.3 V the HIGH level is 2280 mV and the LOW level 1480 mV typical. As a 100-series part the output levels are temperature compensated and stay the same from −40 °C to 85 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Output swing against frequency",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "The output swing is near 800 mV peak to peak at 100 MHz and falls as the toggle rate rises, to roughly 400 mV near 1 GHz and below 150 mV at 1.5 GHz. Random clock jitter stays at 0.2 ps typical, under 1 ps."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Additive phase noise",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "Additive phase noise was measured at 3.3 V and room temperature with an Agilent E5052A analyser and an Agilent E8663B source, at carriers of 25 MHz and 156.25 MHz. Integrated over 12 kHz to 20 MHz, the RMS jitter the device adds is 158 fs at 25 MHz and 48 fs at 156.25 MHz. At 25 MHz the noise settles near −149 dBc/Hz from about 10 kHz offset outward; at 156.25 MHz it is near −148 dBc/Hz from 10 kHz to 100 kHz and near −152 dBc/Hz beyond about 500 kHz."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Exposed pad (DFN8)",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The DFN8 pad is for heat. Give it a thermal path; tie it electrically to GND or leave it unconnected."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Thermal conditions for the limits",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Every limit holds once the device has reached thermal equilibrium, seated in a test socket or soldered to a circuit board, with more than 500 lfpm of airflow across it."
  }
 ],
